Disable pi's self-update on distribution installs.

pi is installed under %{nodejs_sitelib}, i.e. inside a node_modules path, so
detectInstallMethod() returns "npm" and `pi update` would try to run
`npm install -g` over the RPM-owned tree. Returning upstream's own "unknown"
sentinel makes getSelfUpdateCommand() return undefined, which takes the
existing upstream refusal path ("pi cannot self-update this installation.
Update ... using the package manager ... that provides this installation").

Extension/skill/model management (pi install/remove/list, pi update
--extensions/--models) is unaffected; those write to ~/.pi and are the
agent's own tooling, not a self-update.

--- a/dist/config.js	2026-08-11 19:52:24.365730728 +0200
+++ b/dist/config.js	2026-08-11 19:52:24.401734777 +0200
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@
     };
 }
 export function detectInstallMethod() {
+    // openSUSE: this is a distribution package; never self-update.
+    return "unknown";
     if (isBunBinary) {
         return "bun-binary";
     }
